<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John Beattie</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1915–1990</span> · Also known as John H. M. Beattie</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John Beattie was a British social anthropologist at the University of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oxford">Oxford</a>, known for his fieldwork among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banyoro">Nyoro</a> of western Uganda in the 1950s. His books &quot;Bunyoro: An African Kingdom&quot; (1960) and &quot;The Nyoro State&quot; (1971) became standard studies of an African kingdom, and his textbook &quot;Other Cultures&quot; (1964) was widely used.</p></div>
